1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,310
Our dispatchers run 120 trucks.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:07,523
Typing one rate confirmation takes them 5 to 10 minutes.

3
00:00:07,523 --> 00:00:08,995
A CDL, two or three.

4
00:00:08,995 --> 00:00:12,190
And a missing POD can slip by unnoticed.

5
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,567
So we put Meta Muse inside our TMS —

6
00:00:15,567 --> 00:00:19,550
as an agent that does the hunting, and the clicking, for them.

7
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:23,950
Why can't load 4117 be invoiced?

8
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:29,140
Muse checks: the proof of delivery is missing.

9
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:33,330
I switch from Dry run to Live and say: fix it.

10
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,982
Muse drives the app itself —

11
00:00:35,982 --> 00:00:40,130
opens the documents, finds the driver, writes the message…

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,720
…and stops to ask before it presses Send.

13
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,770
I allow it. Sent.

14
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:49,620
Nothing risky happens without a person saying yes.

15
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:53,057
Every load starts with a rate confirmation.

16
00:00:54,067 --> 00:00:57,415
Drop the PDF — Muse fills broker, three stops,

17
00:00:57,415 --> 00:01:01,201
reefer temperature and rate in about seven seconds —

18
00:01:01,201 --> 00:01:04,727
work that takes a dispatcher 5 to 10 minutes.

19
00:01:07,267 --> 00:01:12,521
Hiring: Muse reads a new driver's CDL in 6 seconds instead of 2 or 3 minutes —

20
00:01:12,521 --> 00:01:16,947
and catches that the birth date doesn't match his application.

21
00:01:18,033 --> 00:01:21,253
Most of our drivers speak Uzbek or Russian first.

22
00:01:21,253 --> 00:01:23,233
This one just asks out loud.

23
00:01:23,233 --> 00:01:26,633
[Driver, in Uzbek] When is my next pickup? How many miles are left?

24
00:01:26,633 --> 00:01:29,543
Meta's transcription model doesn't know Uzbek —

25
00:01:29,543 --> 00:01:32,329
but Muse Spark understood the audio directly,

26
00:01:32,329 --> 00:01:35,233
checked his load, and answered him in Uzbek.

27
00:01:35,233 --> 00:01:43,500
[NeWay AI, in Uzbek] Your next pickup: L-4114, Charlotte, today at 4:09 PM Eastern.

28
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:46,683
[NeWay AI, in Uzbek] The load is 405 miles.

29
00:01:46,833 --> 00:01:50,597
Friday, payroll: Muse prepares every driver's statement

30
00:01:50,597 --> 00:01:54,473
and flags what looks wrong — before anyone gets paid.

31
00:01:55,867 --> 00:01:59,453
And every morning, Muse checks the whole fleet on its own:

32
00:01:59,453 --> 00:02:01,680
a load running late, expired papers,

33
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:06,197
and a truck that bought more fuel in an hour than its tanks can hold.

34
00:02:06,767 --> 00:02:08,854
Muse never touches the database.

35
00:02:08,854 --> 00:02:12,443
It calls our own tools with the user's own permissions,

36
00:02:12,443 --> 00:02:15,705
Dry run is on by default, risky presses ask first,

37
00:02:15,705 --> 00:02:17,717
and every write is audited.

38
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:20,895
Built in thirty hours on a TMS

39
00:02:20,895 --> 00:02:24,510
that already runs two real trucking companies.

40
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:32,458
Rate confirmations: 5 to 10 minutes down to 7 seconds.

41
00:02:32,458 --> 00:02:36,840
CDL checks: 2 or 3 minutes down to 6 seconds.

42
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:41,139
Next: dispatchers spend the whole shift searching for loads —

43
00:02:41,139 --> 00:02:46,693
so our next update is a load marketplace where Muse matches empty trucks with freight.

44
00:02:46,693 --> 00:02:47,330
NeWay.
